---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR, GITHUB_URL, GITHUB_REPO_URL } from '../consts';
// Edit the prose below freely. This is your page. Keep it in your own voice.
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${AUTHOR}`}>
  <article class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow fade">About</p>
    <h1><span class="line"><span style="--d:0.06s">Hi, I'm {AUTHOR}.</span></span></h1>

    <div class="prose fade" style="--d:0.2s">
      <p>
        I like running small experiments on open-source and open-weight
        models: how they behave, where they break, and what happens when you
        probe them on safety as well as everyday tasks. Most of what I publish
        here runs locally on a laptop, with programmatic grading documented
        step by step.
      </p>

      <p>
        The audit tooling behind the alignment experiments is open source:
        <a class="u" href={GITHUB_REPO_URL} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">petri-braintrust</a>.
        The smaller local-probe scripts are private for now, but each writeup
        describes its method, prompts, grading rules, sampling settings, in
        enough detail to rebuild it. I'm on
        <a class="u" href={GITHUB_URL} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a> and
        <a class="u" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/paultancre/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.
        The ideas and experiments are mine, built with AI assistance.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* The figure carries the accessible name; the two images are decorative
        alternates of each other, swapped by theme. */}
    <figure class="signature reveal" role="img" aria-label={`${AUTHOR}'s signature`}>
      <img class="sig-light" src="/img/signature-light.png" alt="" width="490" height="264" />
      <img class="sig-dark" src="/img/signature-dark.png" alt="" width="490" height="264" />
    </figure>

    <p class="back mono"><a class="u" href="/">← all experiments</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 1.3rem + 2.2vw, 2.7rem); margin: 0.4rem 0 1.3rem; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .back a { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .back a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
